      "description": "The Cooum flows 72 km through the heart of Chennai from Chembarambakkam reservoir to the Bay of Bengal near Marina Beach. It is one of the most polluted urban rivers in India.",
      "notes": "Over 55 unauthorised sewage outlets drain directly into the Cooum. Dissolved oxygen has been near zero since the early 1990s — the river cannot support any aquatic life and is classified below CPCB Class E. During the 2015 floods, Cooum overflow spread sewage-contaminated water across central Chennai including drinking water infrastructure. Despite multiple High Court and NGT orders mandating restoration, remediation has been minimal.",
