      "cpcb_class": "E (lower reaches below E)",
      "description": "The Adyar flows 42 km from the Chembarambakkam reservoir through southern Chennai to the Bay of Bengal near Adyar Estuary, passing the IIT Madras campus and the Adyar Poonga wetland park.",
      "notes": "The Adyar's upper reaches near Saidapet show slightly higher dissolved oxygen than the Cooum, but degrade sharply near the estuary due to industrial and domestic discharge. During the 2015 floods, floodwaters from the Adyar carried untreated sewage into hundreds of thousands of homes. The Adyar Poonga eco-restoration park has improved a short stretch near Kotturpuram, but the river as a whole remains severely polluted. Industrial effluents from the MEPZ export processing zone contribute to its degradation.",
