      "overall_status": "degraded",
      "cpcb_class": "D–E",
      "description": "The Kosasthalaiyar flows ~90 km through northern Chennai before emptying into Ennore Creek and the Bay of Bengal near Ennore. Its lower reaches pass through India's most heavily industrialised coastal corridor.",
      "notes": "While the Kosasthalaiyar's upper reaches remain comparatively healthier than the Cooum or Adyar, the river deteriorates sharply as it approaches the Ennore industrial zone. Thermal power stations (TNEB North Chennai Thermal Power Station), petrochemical plants (Manali), fertiliser factories, and oil refineries discharge into or adjacent to the river. The Ennore Creek receives fly ash slurry from coal ash ponds, significantly elevating heavy metal concentrations. The National Green Tribunal has issued multiple orders against illegal industrial discharge but compliance has been incomplete.",
